{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
The candles in the win[Bb]dow, the [C]winter [Dm]on the hill
A people long in [C]exile, and wait[A]ing, wait[Gm]ing still
Then o[Dm]ver the dark wa[C]ter there came a [Bb]gentle word
The kindest voice of heaven [C]that ever earth [Dm]had heard
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Comfort, comfort my people, [C]says your [Dm]God
Speak [Bb]tenderly [F]to Je[C]rusalem
In [Dm]the wilderness [Bb]prepare the way of the [C]LORD
Make straight in the [Bb]desert a [C]highway for our [Dm]God
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Every valley shall be lifted up
Every [Bb]mountain and [C]hill made [Dm]low
And the glory of the LORD will be re[C]vealed
And [Bb]all flesh to[C]gether will [Dm]see it
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Comfort, comfort my people, [C]says your [Dm]God
Speak [Bb]tenderly [F]to Je[C]rusalem
In the [Dm]wilderness pre[Bb]pare the way of the [C]LORD
Make straight in the [Bb]desert a [C]highway for our [Dm]God
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
